From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlie <5764343+charlielye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:55:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(world-state): give aztec-wsdb its data directory,
 map sizes and threads in Init's options

aztec-wsdb no longer takes them on its command line: the process and the in-process library are both configured
by Init, whose options carry aztec-wsdb's own msgpack (dataDir, mapSizes as { treeId, sizeKb }, threads).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015HXzMEGRnmFYs5yXRcAWCb

